---
/**
 * /pricing: THE canonical fee page. Every other property (homepage FAQ, blog
 * posts, docs, business, llms.txt) should state fees consistently with this
 * page and link here. Sovereign pricing is enforced by the Ophis backend;
 * hosted pricing remains the CIP-75 flat-fee path.
 *
 * FAQ answers are rendered VERBATIM as the visible section body (the postbuild
 * check-faq-schema gate requires schema text to appear in visible text), so
 * edit the FAQS constants, not the markup.
 */
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro'
import { canonicalPage } from '../data/canonicalPages'
import { SOVEREIGN_CHAIN_LIST as sovereignList } from '../data/chains'

const { updated } = canonicalPage('/pricing/')

const FAQS = [
  {
    q: 'What does Ophis charge?',
    a: `On ${sovereignList}, every path pays a 1 bp base. Ophis retains 80% of reference-quote improvement on volatile pairs, capped at 50 bps of volume, or 50% on stable pairs, capped at 20 bps. CoW-hosted chains retain 10 bps retail, 5 bps partner, and 1 bp stablecoin rates.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the all-in cost on each chain?',
    a: `On ${sovereignList}, the minimum is 1 bp and the maximum Ophis charge is 51 bps on volatile pairs or 21 bps on stable pairs. On CoW-hosted chains, CoW Protocol adds its own fees on top of Ophis's hosted flat fee.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Does Ophis take a cut of surplus?',
    a: `On ${sovereignList}, yes: 80% on volatile pairs or 50% on stable pairs, subject to the caps. The measurement is improvement over the backend reference quote, not the user's slippage limit. On CoW-hosted chains Ophis takes no additional improvement share.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What do integrators pay, and what can they charge?',
    a: `Integrations pay the same 1 bp base plus capped improvement capture on sovereign chains. Hosted integrations retain the 5 bps base, reduced to 1 bp for stable pairs. Integrators can still charge an onboarded own-fee on top.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Are the APIs free?',
    a: `Yes. The public Intent API and the MCP server are free to call. The Intent API is rate-limited to 30 requests per minute per IP; partner-tier rate limits are reviewed case by case.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Are there rebates?',
    a: `Yes. Volume rebate tiers (10% to 50% by rolling 30-day volume) weight your share of a monthly WETH rebate pool, and a referral layer pays 8% or 12% of the net fee Ophis keeps, monthly in WETH, on-chain.`,
  },
]
---

<ContentPage
  title="Ophis fees and pricing"
  description="The canonical Ophis fee reference: 1 bp plus capped price-improvement capture on Ophis-operated chains, with existing flat rates on CoW-hosted chains."
  path="/pricing/"
  heading="Fees and pricing"
  lede="Solver-aligned pricing on Ophis-operated chains and transparent flat rates on hosted chains."
  updated={updated}
  faqs={FAQS}
>
  <p>
    <strong>The short version:</strong> on {sovereignList}, Ophis charges 1 bp plus 80% of
    reference-quote improvement on volatile pairs (50 bps cap), or 50% on stable pairs (20 bps cap).
    Hosted chains retain the existing flat rates.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Path</th>
        <th scope="col">Ophis-operated</th>
        <th scope="col">CoW-hosted</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://swap.ophis.fi/">Swap app</a></td>
        <td>1 bp + 80% improvement (50 bps cap); 50%/20 bps cap for stables</td>
        <td>10 bps retail; 1 bp stables</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://github.com/ophis-fi/ophis/tree/main/packages/sdk">@ophis/sdk</a> integrations</td>
        <td>Same sovereign model</td>
        <td>5 bps partner; 1 bp stables</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/ai-agents">MCP server</a> (keyless)</td>
        <td>Same sovereign model</td>
        <td>5 bps</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Intent API and MCP calls themselves</td>
        <td>Free</td>
        <td>Free</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  {FAQS.map((f) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{f.q}</h2>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>
    On $100,000 of sovereign volatile volume with 20 bps of improvement, Ophis receives $10 base
    plus $160 of improvement capture: $170 total. On a stable pair with the same improvement, the
    stable capture is 10 bps, producing $110 total; the new 20 bps cap does not bind until improvement reaches 40 bps. Hosted-chain costs follow the flat schedule above.
  </p>

  <h2>Sources and detail</h2>
  <p>
    Chain-by-chain fee detail lives at <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/fees">docs.ophis.fi/fees</a>,
    integrator terms at <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/partners">docs.ophis.fi/partners</a> and
    <a href="https://business.ophis.fi/">business.ophis.fi</a>, rebate mechanics at
    <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/affiliate">docs.ophis.fi/affiliate</a>, and CoW Protocol's own
    fee schedule at <a href="https://docs.cow.fi/governance/fees">docs.cow.fi</a>. See also
    <a href="/supported-chains/">supported chains</a> for which chains are Ophis-operated.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
